        "type_uz": "Ichki a'zo",
        "english": "bilaminar disk",
        "translation_uz": "bilaminar disk (Ichki a'zo)",
        "definition_uz": "Anatomik ta'rif (Ichki a'zo): A flattened, almost circular bilaminar plate of cells formed when the inner cell mass (aka embryoblast) forms two epithelial layers, each of a distinct lineage, separated by an extracellular basement membrane: the external (dorsal) layer is called the epiblast and the internal (ventral) layer is called the hypoblast (aka primitive endoderm); together, they compose the bilaminar embryonic disc.",
        "slug": "/structure/bilaminar-disc/",
        "description_en": "A flattened, almost circular bilaminar plate of cells formed when the inner cell mass (aka embryoblast) forms two epithelial layers, each of a distinct lineage, separated by an extracellular basement membrane: the external (dorsal) layer is called the epiblast and the internal (ventral) layer is called the hypoblast (aka primitive endoderm); together, they compose the bilaminar embryonic disc."
