        "translation_uz": "bulbar (Ichki a'zo)",
        "definition_uz": "Anatomik ta'rif (Ichki a'zo): The corticobulbar (or corticonuclear) tract is a white matter pathway connecting the cerebral cortex to the brainstem. The term &#x27;bulbar&#x27; refers to the brainstem, as &#x27;bulb&#x27; was a historical term meaning the area currently called the brainstem. The &#x27;bulb&#x27; is an archaic term for the medulla oblongata. In clinical usage, it includes the pons as well.",
