        "category": "anatomy_organ",
        "type": "Organ",
        "type_uz": "Ichki a'zo",
        "english": "mPFC",
        "translation_uz": "mPFC (Ichki a'zo)",
        "definition_uz": "Anatomik ta'rif (Ichki a'zo): The medial prefrontal cortex (mPFC) is a subdivision of the prefrontal cortex composed of BA12, BA25, and anterior cingulate cortex: BA32, BA33, BA24. Within this region is the dorsal nexus, which interconnects multiple brain networks and plays a role in maintenance and manipulation of information (working memory), as well as supporting the control of cognitive functions such as emotion processing and regulation, memory, decision making, and conflict resolution.",
        "slug": "/structure/medial-prefrontal-cortex/",
        "description_en": "The medial prefrontal cortex (mPFC) is a subdivision of the prefrontal cortex composed of BA12, BA25, and anterior cingulate cortex: BA32, BA33, BA24. Within this region is the dorsal nexus, which interconnects multiple brain networks and plays a role in maintenance and manipulation of information (working memory), as well as supporting the control of cognitive functions such as emotion processing and regulation, memory, decision making, and conflict resolution."
