        "category": "anatomy_bone",
        "type": "Bone",
        "type_uz": "Suyak",
        "english": "3rd digit distal phalanx",
        "translation_uz": "3rd digit distal phalanx (Suyak)",
        "definition_uz": "Anatomik ta'rif (Suyak): A distal phalanx that is part of a digit 3. In odd-toes ungulates (Perissodactyla e.g. horses) this is called the coffin bone. In even-toed ungulates (Artiodactyla e.g cattle) this is associated with the medial claw.",
        "slug": "/structure/distal-phalanx-of-digit-3/",
        "description_en": "A distal phalanx that is part of a digit 3. In odd-toes ungulates (Perissodactyla e.g. horses) this is called the coffin bone. In even-toed ungulates (Artiodactyla e.g cattle) this is associated with the medial claw."
