        "latin": "chorionic terminal villus",
        "category": "anatomy_vessel",
        "type": "Vessel",
        "type_uz": "Qon tomiri",
        "english": "terminal villus",
        "translation_uz": "terminal villus (Qon tomiri)",
        "definition_uz": "Anatomik ta'rif (Qon tomiri): The most distal part of a chorionic villus. A chorionic terminal villus is a grape-like structure characterized by a high degree of capillarization and highly dilated sinusoids. A terminal villus has less stroma and a discontinuous cytotrophoblast layer, and contains 4–6 fetal capillaries per cross section. It exhibits a diameter ranging from 40 to about 80 μm.",
        "slug": "/structure/chorionic-terminal-villus/",
        "description_en": "The most distal part of a chorionic villus. A chorionic terminal villus is a grape-like structure characterized by a high degree of capillarization and highly dilated sinusoids. A terminal villus has less stroma and a discontinuous cytotrophoblast layer, and contains 4–6 fetal capillaries per cross section. It exhibits a diameter ranging from 40 to about 80 μm."
