        "latin": "thyroid follicular lumen",
        "category": "anatomy_gland",
        "type": "Gland",
        "type_uz": "Bez",
        "english": "follicular lumen",
        "translation_uz": "follicular lumen (Bez)",
        "definition_uz": "Anatomik ta'rif (Bez): A follicular lumen is the closed cavity within a follicle of the thyroid gland. It is surrounded by follicular cells and filled with colloid, a concentrated solution of thyroglobulin.",
